<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ellac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 454</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ellac was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>. Around 448 Attila made him king over the Akatziri, a people north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. After Attila's death in 453 his sons quarrelled over the inheritance, and their subject peoples, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardaric">Ardaric</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, rose in revolt. Ellac was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao">Battle of Nedao</a> in 454, and Hunnic power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ellac.jpg" alt="Ellac" width="229" height="289" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mór Than · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Son_of_Attila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
